The Rust lexical path parsing, joining and existence checks in this directory
adapt CPython v3.13.15 Lib/pathlib/__init__.py, Lib/posixpath.py,
Lib/ntpath.py and PC/errmap.h. Changes: owned UTF-8 path components and Rust
filesystem metadata replace Python objects; native Windows execution and
arbitrary non-UTF-8 path behavior are not established by these adaptations.

The archive file-URL adapter in plugin/index/transport/file_url and shared
URL-parts adapter in plugin/index/transport/url_parts also adapt CPython
v3.13.15 Lib/urllib/parse.py, Lib/urllib/request.py and Lib/nturl2path.py.
Changes: Rust strings, percent decoding and native paths replace Python objects;
Unix UTF-8/surrogateescape conversion is represented directly as filesystem bytes.
The NFKC delimiter classification is pinned to Unicode 15.1 rather than a host
normalization library. Windows conversion is compared through pure path objects;
native Windows filesystem execution is not established by that comparison.

The catalogue redirect target adapter in plugin/index/github/redirect/target.rs
also adapts CPython v3.13.15 Lib/urllib/parse.py and Lib/urllib/request.py.
Changes: Rust owned URL components and byte headers replace Python objects;
request transport remains separate from lexical target construction.

The catalogue file handler in plugin/index/github/file also adapts CPython
v3.13.15 Lib/urllib/request.py, Lib/urllib/parse.py and Lib/nturl2path.py.
Changes: Python code-point strings, Rust filesystem objects and native IPv4
resolution preserve request/path/open boundaries without pathlib normalization.
Native Windows operations and alternate filesystem/DNS codec profiles remain
separate runtime verification requirements.

The catalogue file-header timestamp adapter in plugin/index/github/file/headers
also adapts CPython v3.13.15 Python/pytime.c, Modules/_datetimemodule.c and
Modules/posixmodule.c. Changes: native Rust timestamp values and platform calendar
calls replace Python objects; header consumers preserve the source error classes.
The observed macOS ARM64 stat conversion uses fused binary64 multiplication and
addition; other compiler contraction profiles require separate verification.

